

In Christian theology and the New Testament, Christ's power and authority over demons and unclean spirits is commonly referred to as spiritual authority or divine authority (often paired with spiritual power or deliverance).
In biblical passages like Luke 4:36 and Mark 1:27, onlookers describe Jesus commanding unclean spirits with authority and power. Within Christian teaching, these terms are often distinguished:
• Authority (exousia): The legal right, supreme rule, or right to command and be obeyed.
• Power (dynamis): The ability, strength, or spiritual enablement to carry out that command.
When exercised to drive out evil spirits, the act is commonly called exorcism or deliverance